    "rationale": "Anderson acceleration with least-squares secant updates is inherently unsuitable for fixed-displacement Alternating Minimization in the softening regime without global line search or arc-length control. Secant combinations of past iterates extrapolate outside the local basin of attraction when the elastic-phase potential landscape lacks strong convexity. A parameter sweep (e.g. Anderson depth m or trust-region delta) is scientifically unwarranted because standard monotonic AM already reaches Delta d = 0.001187, and nonstationarity at Increment 87 is governed by physical softening localization, not algorithmic deficiency."
